This reports the wrong length for anything this service stored in parts (over 8 MiB). The multipart client hands back part 1's response, so a 20 MiB obs reports 8388608 where master's HEAD gave 20971520. I reproduced it on LocalStack; S3Mock ignores `partNumber`, so the IT can't see it. legacyui's [`ComplexObsServlet`](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-legacyui/blob/master/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/servlet/ComplexObsServlet.java) sends this as Content-Length, so the download comes back truncated.

```suggestion
		metadata.setLength(getObjectLength(getResponse));
		return new DataWithMetadata(response, metadata);
	}

	/**
	 * With multipart enabled the client downloads in parts and hands back the first part's response, so
	 * Content-Length is that part's size, while Content-Range ends with the size of the object.
	 */
	private Long getObjectLength(GetObjectResponse response) {
		String total = StringUtils.substringAfterLast(response.contentRange(), "/");
		return StringUtils.isNumeric(total) ? Long.valueOf(total) : response.contentLength();
	}
```

Legacy obs with long non-ASCII titles stop loading. Before 2.8 files were named `<title>_<uuid>.<ext>`, and `encodeKey` turns each non-ASCII byte into `%XX`, so a 36-letter Cyrillic title pushes the encoded name past 255 bytes. The stat then fails with "File name too long" rather than `NoSuchFileException`, and the legacy file master still reads is never tried. Falling back on any `FileSystemException` fixes it (it also needs `import java.nio.file.FileSystemException;`, and the `NoSuchFileException` import goes unused):

```suggestion
	private <T> T read(String key, IOFunction<Path, T> reader) throws IOException {
		Path path = storageDir.resolve(encodeKey(key));
		FileSystemException currentLocationFailure = null;
		if (isInStorageDir(path)) {
			try {
				return reader.apply(path);
			} catch (FileSystemException e) {
				// Not only a missing file: a legacy name the encoding pushes past the file system's name
				// length limit fails here too, so the legacy location decides
				currentLocationFailure = e;
			}
		}

		Path legacyPath = getLegacyStorageDir().resolve(key);
		if (fileExists(legacyPath)) {
			assertKeyInLegacyStorageDir(legacyPath, key);
			return reader.apply(legacyPath);
		}

		if (currentLocationFailure != null) {
			throw currentLocationFailure;
		}
		throw new IllegalArgumentException("Key must not point outside storage dir. Wrong key: " + key);
	}
```

This needs to reach the bundled handlers before merge, since they are what [TRUNK-6682](https://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/TRUNK-6682)'s call-count criterion guards. All five override `AbstractHandler.getObs`, so putting `storageService.exists(key)` back into `BinaryStreamHandler`, or a separate `getMetadata` into the other four, leaves every test green. Each handler's test could run its own `getObs` against `CountingStorageService`, moved to its own file:

```java
ImageHandler handler = new ImageHandler();
ReflectionTestUtils.setField(handler, "adminService", adminService);
ReflectionTestUtils.setField(handler, "storageService", counting);
```

